1
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,000
No ! I can 't concentrate .

2
00:00:34,458 --> 00:00:36,458
Please , maestro I 'm sorry but ...

3
00:00:36,583 --> 00:00:39,042
Let 's continue from number 37 .

4
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:11,458
Oh , my god ! No , no !

5
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:15,208
Maestro , please let 's take it from " Vieni Altrove "

6
00:01:32,625 --> 00:01:34,542
Stop ! Stop !

7
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,125
I can 't stand it anymore !

8
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:42,208
- It 's ridiculous ! - Poor thing . Are you hurt ?

9
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:45,500
It 's ridiculous ! This is Macbeth by Giuseppe Verdi !

10
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:47,667
I 've never seen such lousy direction .

11
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:51,417
- Is there a problem ? - Yes , you director !

12
00:01:51,625 --> 00:01:53,916
This isn 't one of your third rate movies !

13
00:01:53,951 --> 00:01:56,208
Birds on stage , back projection , laser beams !

14
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:58,208
Is this an opera or amusement park ?

15
00:01:58,375 --> 00:02:00,625
I have to sing ! How can I do that

16
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:02,875
with a raven on stage that hates me ?

17
00:02:03,042 --> 00:02:04,840
Why would the raven hate you ?

18
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:06,792
It always looks at me with those eyes ..

19
00:02:06,917 --> 00:02:10,250
It shrieks , whistles , flaps its wings .

20
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:12,417
It 's deliberately disturbs my performance

21
00:02:12,452 --> 00:02:14,382
I won 't be back !

22
00:02:14,417 --> 00:02:15,458
But it 's just an animal ...

23
00:02:15,493 --> 00:02:16,590
That 's right !

24
00:02:16,625 --> 00:02:18,792
Animals shouldn 't be at the Opera

25
00:02:18,827 --> 00:02:20,583
singing Macbeth !

26
00:02:20,792 --> 00:02:22,208
- Where is my manager ? - I 'm here Mara .

27
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:24,667
Where is my manager ? I am going back to the hotel .

28
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,632
- Please don 't be like this . - It 's 4 : 30 ...

29
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:29,167
I 'll rest until 7 : 00 and at 8 : 00 I 'll be ready to sing .

30
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:31,500
Without ravens or any other nonsense !

31
00:02:31,625 --> 00:02:33,417
A real opera !

32
00:02:33,625 --> 00:02:35,417
What do we do now ?

33
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,500
Let 's get on with the rehearsal .

34
00:02:37,833 --> 00:02:39,667
If something like this happens again

35
00:02:39,702 --> 00:02:41,583
I 'll take my ravens and leave .

36
00:02:41,618 --> 00:02:42,632
OK .

37
00:02:42,667 --> 00:02:44,396
Maestro ? Let 's get back to it .

38
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:46,125
We 'll take it from we left it .

39
00:02:56,083 --> 00:02:57,590
This is all your fault

40
00:02:57,625 --> 00:02:59,542
for such a bizarre and outrageous direction !

41
00:03:00,458 --> 00:03:02,833
Ladies and gentlemen , the great Mara Chekova

42
00:03:02,868 --> 00:03:04,208
Has been knocked down by a car !

43
00:03:04,292 --> 00:03:06,750
Call an ambulance . Hurry !

44
00:03:06,833 --> 00:03:08,500
Go ! Run ! Hurry !

45
00:03:08,917 --> 00:03:11,750
Oh God ! Oh God ! What a disaster !

46
00:03:51,042 --> 00:03:53,042
- Hello ? - Is that you , Betty ?

47
00:03:53,125 --> 00:03:54,132
Yes .

48
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:56,667
Tonight you make your debut as Lady Macbeth .

49
00:03:56,702 --> 00:03:58,708
- What ? - Are you happy ?

50
00:03:59,167 --> 00:04:00,500
Who 's speaking ?

51
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:04,583
Is this a joke ?

52
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:07,875
Hello ?

53
00:04:09,083 --> 00:04:10,667
Hello ?

54
00:05:01,125 --> 00:05:02,167
Mira !

55
00:05:02,208 --> 00:05:04,167
Come on , Betty .

56
00:05:04,542 --> 00:05:06,917
Get ready , in exactly one hour , you 've got to be on stage .

57
00:05:07,125 --> 00:05:09,792
Mara Chekova had an accident . Here .

58
00:05:10,292 --> 00:05:13,250
Someone already called . I thought it was a joke .

59
00:05:13,375 --> 00:05:14,840
Why are you crying ?

60
00:05:14,875 --> 00:05:16,833
Are you scared of making your debut ?

61
00:05:17,458 --> 00:05:20,167
No ! But I 'm too young for Lady Macbeth .

62
00:05:20,202 --> 00:05:21,590
My voice isn 't right .

63
00:05:21,625 --> 00:05:24,125
No , you 'll make a sensation !

64
00:05:24,792 --> 00:05:26,500
I won 't be able to reach some of the notes .

65
00:05:26,535 --> 00:05:28,090
- I can 't do it ! - Trust me .

66
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:29,833
I 'm not just your agent , I 'm also your friend .

67
00:05:30,042 --> 00:05:31,917
I know what you 're going through .

68
00:05:31,952 --> 00:05:33,542
Just stage fright .

69
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,173
Don 't let them see it .

70
00:05:35,208 --> 00:05:37,250
They 're all here to see you .

71
00:05:37,542 --> 00:05:40,042
Don 't show them your lack of confidence

72
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:41,250
All right ! I get it !

73
00:05:42,458 --> 00:05:44,875
Well , my dear Betty , are we ready ?

74
00:05:45,042 --> 00:05:47,167
Mara 's unfortunate accident is going

75
00:05:47,202 --> 00:05:49,292
to speed you towards your destiny .

76
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,792
Tonight you will make your debut in Verdi 's Macbeth .

77
00:05:52,458 --> 00:05:53,833
What are those tears ?

78
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:55,792
Tears of happiness , I hope .

79
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,583
Don 't tell me you 're afraid .

80
00:05:57,618 --> 00:05:58,750
Afraid you 'll fail ?

81
00:05:58,917 --> 00:06:00,625
I 'm too young for the role .

82
00:06:01,542 --> 00:06:03,083
Did you know that Verdi 's first Lady Macbeth

83
00:06:03,118 --> 00:06:04,792
was only 17 ?

84
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:07,625
Anyway , you know the opera by heart .

85
00:06:07,792 --> 00:06:11,625
I watched you at all rehearsals . You worked so hard ...

86
00:06:11,792 --> 00:06:14,750
As though you were the star and not the understudy .

87
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:19,458
Don 't worry about the orchestra .

88
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,333
They 'll only need half an hour 's rehearsal .

89
00:06:21,375 --> 00:06:22,375
Excellent .

90
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:24,833
Come on . Stop it ! This is your big chance .

91
00:06:25,042 --> 00:06:26,667
I know but ...

92
00:06:27,250 --> 00:06:28,604
Think of how happy and proud

93
00:06:28,639 --> 00:06:29,958
your mother would have been ...

94
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,542
if she saw you following in her footsteps .

95
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,792
That would have pleased her .

96
00:06:34,827 --> 00:06:36,208
Believe me .

97
00:06:37,792 --> 00:06:39,333
What happened to Chekova ?

98
00:06:39,875 --> 00:06:42,542
She got hit by a car or so I heard .

99
00:06:43,583 --> 00:06:47,125
Ah , you are listening to Prokofsky 's recording of Macbeth .

100
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:49,375
Did you know it was a production of ours ?

101
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,667
1975 .

102
00:06:51,583 --> 00:06:54,375
It 's the opera . Macbeth brings bad luck .

103
00:06:54,875 --> 00:06:56,632
What are you talking about ?

104
00:06:56,667 --> 00:06:59,833
Everyone says it . It 's a beautiful opera but ...

105
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,417
it brings bad luck ...

106
00:07:01,667 --> 00:07:04,333
I would much rather make my debut in something else .

107
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,750
Don 't let them hear you say that .

108
00:07:05,785 --> 00:07:07,208
- But it 's true ! - Shut up !

109
00:07:07,375 --> 00:07:09,417
So you think this opera brings bad luck ?

110
00:07:09,667 --> 00:07:11,667
I don 't know . It 's what everyone says .

111
00:07:11,792 --> 00:07:13,298
I don 't say it .

112
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:15,917
Listen , you have a wonderful voice .

113
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,583
You are very beautiful

114
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:19,298
and you 're lucky enough

115
00:07:19,333 --> 00:07:21,250
to be making your debut in a great theater .

116
00:07:21,375 --> 00:07:23,708
You should make the most of this opportunity .

117
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,542
These things usually only happen

118
00:07:26,577 --> 00:07:28,042
to people in movies .

119
00:07:29,458 --> 00:07:32,583
Just seize the opportunity and stop being silly .

120
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
OK .

121
00:07:35,167 --> 00:07:36,167
Good call .

122
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:20,667
Six , five , four , three , two , one , now !

123
00:09:25,917 --> 00:09:28,458
Let her through , let her through !

124
00:09:34,417 --> 00:09:36,167
There 's too much smoke .

125
00:09:37,208 --> 00:09:38,917
I said there 's too much smoke !

126
00:09:39,042 --> 00:09:41,167
Dino , cut the smoke . Cut the smoke !

127
00:09:41,375 --> 00:09:44,250
Wait a second . No ! The scar should be on the other side !

128
00:09:44,583 --> 00:09:46,340
Betty goes on in two minutes !

129
00:09:46,375 --> 00:09:47,750
Good , another two minutes for Betty .

130
00:09:47,785 --> 00:09:49,000
Go back , hurry !

131
00:09:49,917 --> 00:09:51,708
Betty , you 're on in two minutes .

132
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:55,792
Put it on better ! I told you to turn it !

133
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,167
Oh , what are you doing ? Leave it !

134
00:09:58,417 --> 00:10:02,208
- Oh , no , stop it ! - It will be a success !

135
00:10:02,243 --> 00:10:04,250
Break a leg !

136
00:10:04,708 --> 00:10:06,708
That 's okay . I 'll just do it myself .

137
00:10:32,375 --> 00:10:35,250
Be careful ! Don 't ruin the costume .

138
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,417
You 've finally returned .

139
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:57,792
What are you doing here ? You 're not allowed in here .

140
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:02,708
This box is for stage personnel only . Come on . Let 's go .

141
00:14:15,375 --> 00:14:16,667
Are you mad ?

142
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:37,042
Betty , let 's continue .

143
00:14:37,250 --> 00:14:39,417
Keep going !

144
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:42,375
It was an accident . Nothing more . Okay ?

145
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,458
Give it here .

146
00:14:47,417 --> 00:14:48,667
All good , maestro .

147
00:16:58,167 --> 00:17:01,167
Well done , Betty ! You 're so wonderful !

148
00:17:02,875 --> 00:17:06,583
Enough ! Enough ! That idiot !

149
00:17:07,583 --> 00:17:11,125
That 's enough , Mara ! Don 't be childish .

150
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:13,458
What a triumph ! You 're a star !

151
00:17:13,667 --> 00:17:14,632
You really think so ?

152
00:17:14,667 --> 00:17:16,708
Didn 't you hear the applause ?

153
00:17:16,875 --> 00:17:17,875
Thank you .

154
00:17:18,917 --> 00:17:20,896
Bravo . You 're wonderful ! Wonderful !

155
00:17:20,931 --> 00:17:22,875
Congratulations ! . You were magnificent .

156
00:17:22,910 --> 00:17:23,875
Thank you .

157
00:17:25,875 --> 00:17:27,875
There 'll be a reception later on .

158
00:17:27,910 --> 00:17:29,875
- Don 't miss it ! - Thank you .

159
00:17:30,125 --> 00:17:34,083
- Betty , you were perfect . - I owe to you , maestro .

160
00:17:34,208 --> 00:17:36,625
- Will I see you at the reception ? - Yes . Of course .

161
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:37,632
A real triumph !

162
00:17:37,667 --> 00:17:39,500
Marc , the press are here .

163
00:17:39,542 --> 00:17:41,542
Yes , there was an accident with the lights .

164
00:17:42,292 --> 00:17:44,042
I hear shouting and screaming in the room !

165
00:17:44,167 --> 00:17:45,458
What are you talking about , what screams ?

166
00:17:45,583 --> 00:17:47,125
- You didn 't hear it ? - No .

167
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:49,167
Yes , it came from one of the boxes .

168
00:17:49,202 --> 00:17:51,500
- Betty ? - Oh , Marc !

169
00:17:57,708 --> 00:18:02,250
I know we 've had a little accident , but it 's got nothing to do with Macbeth .

170
00:18:02,375 --> 00:18:05,333
The only bad luck Macbeth has brought you is fame .

171
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:08,750
My mother was a famous singer as well .

172
00:18:08,833 --> 00:18:10,548
Betty , go change quickly .

173
00:18:10,583 --> 00:18:13,167
People will be waiting for you . Hurry !

174
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:22,000
Fantastic !

175
00:18:29,417 --> 00:18:30,792
Everything was perfect !

176
00:18:30,827 --> 00:18:32,167
Betty , you were fantastic !

177
00:18:32,202 --> 00:18:33,750
You were great !

178
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:36,292
I just love Verdi 's music . I really do !

179
00:18:36,542 --> 00:18:39,500
You were wonderful . Just wonderful .

180
00:18:39,708 --> 00:18:42,750
It 's just that damn , damn director !

181
00:18:42,785 --> 00:18:44,917
I can 't take him anymore .

182
00:18:49,625 --> 00:18:51,625
Giulia ?

183
00:18:54,333 --> 00:18:56,083
You work here in the theater ?

184
00:18:56,833 --> 00:18:58,375
No ... l ...

185
00:19:01,708 --> 00:19:04,708
- You 're a fan of mine . - Yes .

186
00:19:04,917 --> 00:19:06,500
The first .

187
00:19:06,833 --> 00:19:08,500
- Sorry ? - My first ... fan .

188
00:19:08,875 --> 00:19:10,000
Congratulations .

189
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:14,083
- Do you want an autograph ? - Oh , yeah .

190
00:19:14,208 --> 00:19:17,500
- That 's very nice of you . Thank you . - Don 't mention it .

191
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,375
What name shall I write ? Excuse me .

192
00:19:23,458 --> 00:19:24,833
Alan .

193
00:19:25,042 --> 00:19:27,500
Alan ?

194
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:33,375
- Thank you . - Are you a foreigner ?

195
00:19:33,410 --> 00:19:34,500
Oh , no .

196
00:19:34,708 --> 00:19:36,917
Everything is ready , Inspector , and they 're all waiting for you .

197
00:19:37,042 --> 00:19:38,125
Yes I 'm coming .

198
00:19:38,208 --> 00:19:40,125
So you are a policeman , not a fan .

199
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:43,875
Can 't a policeman be a fan ? It 's just that ...

200
00:19:44,292 --> 00:19:47,750
I 'm not an expert on opera but ...

201
00:19:48,125 --> 00:19:50,542
Your voice is ...

202
00:19:52,458 --> 00:19:54,458
Thanks for the autograph .

203
00:19:58,542 --> 00:20:00,208
Yes ?

204
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:01,465
- Hi . - Hi .

205
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,167
- What did the cop want ? - Nothing , just my autograph .

206
00:20:04,250 --> 00:20:06,250
But who knows what he is doing here ?

207
00:20:06,375 --> 00:20:08,042
I don 't know . I have no idea .

208
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:10,298
Oh , maybe because of the accident

209
00:20:10,333 --> 00:20:11,875
with the lights . One of the ushers died .

210
00:20:12,042 --> 00:20:14,042
- What ? - Yes , it 's very strange .

211
00:20:14,167 --> 00:20:16,548
Leave your costume there .

212
00:20:16,583 --> 00:20:19,125
Marc says it needs a few alterations .

213
00:20:19,292 --> 00:20:21,083
Listen Stefano , I don 't want to go to the party alone .

214
00:20:21,118 --> 00:20:22,423
Would you come with me ?

215
00:20:22,458 --> 00:20:24,375
- Please ? - Of course , I would love to !

216
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:27,250
I almost forgot . You were great tonight .

217
00:20:28,125 --> 00:20:29,667
And it looks like I 'm the last one

218
00:20:29,702 --> 00:20:31,042
to congratulate you .

219
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:32,500
So you think it would be okay if I had a kiss ?

220
00:20:32,535 --> 00:20:34,750
Even if I 'm only the stage manager ?

221
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:36,542
Can I ?

222
00:20:43,292 --> 00:20:44,833
Did you really like me ? Really ?

223
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,917
Like you ? I loved you ! You were great .

224
00:20:48,667 --> 00:20:51,167
From the great Mara Chekova .

225
00:20:53,375 --> 00:20:55,833
- With her best wishes . - Thank you .

226
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,875
The great Mara Chekova ..

227
00:21:03,083 --> 00:21:05,250
We can say that she was literally struck

228
00:21:05,285 --> 00:21:06,500
by the curse of Macbeth .

229
00:21:09,917 --> 00:21:12,208
" Good luck , little snake . "

230
00:21:13,333 --> 00:21:14,375
Bitch .

231
00:21:14,625 --> 00:21:16,375
Hmm ... What is it ?

232
00:21:16,667 --> 00:21:18,083
How should I know ?

233
00:21:30,167 --> 00:21:32,667
- What do you think it is ? - Who knows ?

234
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:35,250
Snake venom ?

235
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:38,667
Acid ? Toad slime ?

236
00:21:47,917 --> 00:21:50,458
Hey ! Stefano ! What 's wrong ?

237
00:21:50,583 --> 00:21:52,833
What 's happening ? What 's happening ?

238
00:21:54,458 --> 00:21:55,917
You idiot !

239
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,042
You scared me .

240
00:21:58,292 --> 00:21:59,500
But what was it ?

241
00:21:59,750 --> 00:22:04,292
Yuck ! Ginseng ! Chekova would bathe in that stuff !

242
00:27:51,292 --> 00:27:52,500
Stop this racket !

243
00:27:52,667 --> 00:27:54,625
Filthy damn birds !

244
00:28:25,125 --> 00:28:28,542
No , it 's useless . I can 't . It 's not your fault .

245
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:31,007
I 'm a disaster in bed .

246
00:28:31,042 --> 00:28:32,917
I don 't know why . I 'm sorry .

247
00:28:33,917 --> 00:28:35,882
According to the legend

248
00:28:35,917 --> 00:28:37,750
opera singers are incredibly horny .

249
00:28:37,875 --> 00:28:39,917
I 'm serious . They say they make love

250
00:28:39,952 --> 00:28:41,601
before they go on stage .

251
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:43,250
It makes the voice ...

252
00:28:43,750 --> 00:28:47,083
The voice more relaxed ... free

253
00:28:47,708 --> 00:28:49,583
Either I 'm a lousy opera singer ...

254
00:28:50,458 --> 00:28:52,125
Or I am an exception .

255
00:28:52,333 --> 00:28:54,250
- Have I offended you ? - No .

256
00:28:55,292 --> 00:28:58,632
Well , I mean ... now that you 're famous

257
00:28:58,667 --> 00:29:01,292
it seems that things have changed between us .

258
00:29:01,750 --> 00:29:03,792
No , don 't say that .

259
00:29:03,827 --> 00:29:05,458
It 's not true .

260
00:29:09,708 --> 00:29:11,541
What a beautiful house !

261
00:29:11,576 --> 00:29:13,375
It looks like a museum .

262
00:29:14,083 --> 00:29:17,250
It sort of is . It 's my uncle 's .

263
00:29:17,625 --> 00:29:19,916
He 's a bit crazy but he is really rich

264
00:29:19,951 --> 00:29:22,208
and he lets me use it whenever I need it .

265
00:29:24,333 --> 00:29:26,792
- Want some tea ? - Yes , please .

266
00:29:28,458 --> 00:29:31,917
All right , I 've got rose , jasmine

267
00:29:32,042 --> 00:29:34,292
- Or mint . - Jasmine .

268
00:29:34,327 --> 00:29:35,875
Jasmine . Okay .

269
00:29:47,833 --> 00:29:49,167
No ! Mint !

270
00:31:01,292 --> 00:31:03,917
Take a good look . You can 't close your eyes .

271
00:31:03,952 --> 00:31:07,083
You have to watch everything .

272
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:10,125
Everything .

273
00:31:14,083 --> 00:31:15,208
Betty !

274
00:31:15,917 --> 00:31:19,458
Why did you lock it ? Aren 't you feeling well ?

275
00:31:21,417 --> 00:31:22,833
No , no !

276
00:31:22,875 --> 00:31:24,875
What is going on Betty ?

277
00:31:35,208 --> 00:31:36,417
Oh my God ...

278
00:32:42,667 --> 00:32:45,542
It 's not true you 're frigid .

279
00:32:45,577 --> 00:32:47,792
You 're a bitch on heat .

280
00:33:57,125 --> 00:33:58,715
Hello ?

281
00:33:58,750 --> 00:34:00,583
There 's been a murder .

282
00:34:00,792 --> 00:34:03,750
At 66 Viale Pegaso .

283
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:05,833
Who 's speaking ?

284
00:34:06,917 --> 00:34:08,542
Who 's speaking ?

285
00:34:38,417 --> 00:34:41,833
My god ! Look what success has done to you !

286
00:34:42,250 --> 00:34:43,750
Come on . I 'm gonna get the papers .

287
00:34:43,785 --> 00:34:44,833
I want to read the reviews .

288
00:34:47,667 --> 00:34:48,875
So ?

289
00:34:52,750 --> 00:34:54,583
Is something wrong with your eyes ?

290
00:34:55,458 --> 00:34:56,708
Can I know what 's wrong ?

291
00:34:56,792 --> 00:34:57,875
Yes , the lights .

292
00:34:58,083 --> 00:34:59,979
Oh come on , the lights ?

293
00:35:00,014 --> 00:35:01,944
Okay , it wasn 't the lights .

294
00:35:01,979 --> 00:35:03,875
How do you turn the heating on ?

295
00:35:04,083 --> 00:35:05,083
I 'll do it .

296
00:35:13,417 --> 00:35:16,708
So , will you tell me what happened ?

297
00:35:17,042 --> 00:35:18,708
Nothing . Nothing happened .

298
00:35:18,743 --> 00:35:20,125
It was so ...

299
00:35:21,375 --> 00:35:24,500
No , I can 't tell you .

300
00:35:24,917 --> 00:35:26,500
Trouble in love ?

301
00:35:26,875 --> 00:35:28,458
Love ?

302
00:35:28,542 --> 00:35:30,500
What love ?

303
00:35:30,875 --> 00:35:33,000
Whenever a woman has a problem

304
00:35:33,035 --> 00:35:35,125
men always assume it 's love .

305
00:35:35,250 --> 00:35:37,458
You sopranos are famous for ...

306
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:39,840
For whoring around ?

307
00:35:39,875 --> 00:35:41,875
No , wait a minute ... I didn 't mean that ...

308
00:35:42,083 --> 00:35:45,500
Look , I 've already heard that story tonight .

309
00:35:46,250 --> 00:35:47,750
There 's a bunch of people that think

310
00:35:47,785 --> 00:35:48,715
that we singers ...

311
00:35:48,750 --> 00:35:49,917
make love just before going on stage

312
00:35:49,952 --> 00:35:51,458
to improve our voice .

313
00:35:52,292 --> 00:35:56,167
It 's wrong . For me , anyway , it 's totally wrong .

314
00:35:56,625 --> 00:35:58,542
I don 't understand why you 're so upset .

315
00:35:58,750 --> 00:36:00,708
I don 't want to talk about it .

316
00:36:03,083 --> 00:36:04,083
I don 't know ...

317
00:36:05,208 --> 00:36:07,292
This whole thing just tires me .

318
00:36:08,417 --> 00:36:10,500
Sorry but what 's it got to do with me ?

319
00:36:11,208 --> 00:36:13,000
Why don 't we talk about you instead ?

320
00:36:13,167 --> 00:36:16,167
You film people are known to be a depraved lot ...

321
00:36:16,625 --> 00:36:18,167
Ah that 's for sure .

322
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:22,083
We only work if there is some spare time ...

323
00:36:24,333 --> 00:36:28,500
Come on . You have to talk about it sooner or later .

324
00:36:48,417 --> 00:36:50,583
And then I ran away , and that 's when I found you .

325
00:36:56,167 --> 00:36:57,167
You see ...

326
00:36:57,875 --> 00:37:00,917
The strangest thing about what happened tonight ...

327
00:37:02,250 --> 00:37:03,875
All the terrible things I saw are part of a nightmare

328
00:37:03,910 --> 00:37:05,625
I used to have as a child .

329
00:37:08,458 --> 00:37:10,132
I used to dream of a man

330
00:37:10,167 --> 00:37:12,375
wearing a black hood on his face .

331
00:37:14,500 --> 00:37:16,250
Tonight I saw that same hood .

332
00:37:16,333 --> 00:37:18,667
- You said you called the police . - Yes .

333
00:37:19,042 --> 00:37:21,292
- Did you give your name ? - No .

334
00:37:24,042 --> 00:37:25,333
Did you tell them everything ?

335
00:37:26,167 --> 00:37:28,500
About what happened tonight ? Yes .

336
00:37:28,917 --> 00:37:30,542
Why ? ls there anything else ?

337
00:37:44,833 --> 00:37:46,833
I 'll check all the other rooms .

338
00:37:58,333 --> 00:37:59,792
Have you got a boyfriend ?

339
00:38:01,625 --> 00:38:03,166
- No . - Or someone

340
00:38:03,201 --> 00:38:04,708
who might get jealous ?

341
00:38:04,833 --> 00:38:06,792
No . No one that I know of . Why ?

342
00:38:07,167 --> 00:38:08,257
There 's someone in the street

343
00:38:08,292 --> 00:38:09,750
watching your windows with binoculars .

344
00:38:10,042 --> 00:38:11,917
- Where ? - Come and see .

345
00:38:16,667 --> 00:38:17,875
I don 't see anyone .

346
00:38:18,250 --> 00:38:19,340
Ah , he 's gone .

347
00:38:19,375 --> 00:38:21,458
He was there , next to the photo booth .

348
00:38:44,292 --> 00:38:45,750
Betty , do you want me to stay ?

349
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:49,833
Don 't you have anyone jealous waiting for you ?

350
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:52,292
Yes ... But if you want ...

351
00:38:52,500 --> 00:38:55,250
She must be upset that you 're not home yet .

352
00:38:57,292 --> 00:38:59,750
I 'll lock myself in . Don 't worry .

353
00:39:00,125 --> 00:39:02,333
Make sure you lock all the windows .

354
00:39:02,667 --> 00:39:04,542
I 'll look around in the street .

355
00:39:04,750 --> 00:39:07,375
If I see anything suspicious , I 'll call you .

356
00:39:07,542 --> 00:39:08,542
If not ...

357
00:39:09,417 --> 00:39:11,250
I 'll see you tomorrow .

358
00:39:12,917 --> 00:39:13,917
What 's wrong ?

359
00:39:17,750 --> 00:39:19,000
There are 2 people out there .

360
00:39:19,208 --> 00:39:21,792
- Do you know them ? - No .

361
00:39:23,542 --> 00:39:25,083
Who 's out there ?

362
00:39:26,708 --> 00:39:27,750
Who are you ?

363
00:39:28,542 --> 00:39:30,417
Who do you think it is , I live here !

364
00:39:30,452 --> 00:39:31,917
I 'm your neighbour .

365
00:39:32,083 --> 00:39:34,167
Who is that ? Was he looking for me ?

366
00:39:34,333 --> 00:39:35,500
No .

367
00:39:35,667 --> 00:39:36,798
Don 't be nosy .

368
00:39:36,833 --> 00:39:38,333
Mind your own business .

369
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:40,000
Who are you looking for ?

370
00:39:42,125 --> 00:39:44,000
Do you think it 's true ? I don 't know her .

371
00:39:44,083 --> 00:39:46,333
Maybe she is saying the truth .

372
00:40:05,208 --> 00:40:08,042
Close the door well . I don 't want to lose another Lady Macbeth .

373
00:40:08,125 --> 00:40:09,458
Okay .

374
00:41:37,792 --> 00:41:39,083
Who is it ?

375
00:41:40,125 --> 00:41:41,583
Who 's there ?

376
00:41:46,542 --> 00:41:47,708
Who is it ?

377
00:41:51,917 --> 00:41:53,375
Hello ?

378
00:41:54,917 --> 00:41:56,792
Who is there ? Who is speaking ?

379
00:41:58,833 --> 00:42:01,208
Marc ? Is that you ?

380
00:42:10,208 --> 00:42:13,583
Oh , my god ! Why did I do it ?

381
00:42:13,667 --> 00:42:16,208
I shouldn 't have accepted the role .

382
00:42:20,250 --> 00:42:22,083
It 's all my fault .

383
00:42:25,583 --> 00:42:28,125
Why , why did I do it ?

384
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:44,500
Don 't cry , Betty . Don 't cry .

385
00:42:45,625 --> 00:42:48,125
" Hostile reception for Macbeth . "

386
00:42:48,667 --> 00:42:50,757
" Brilliant debut by a young singer ...

387
00:42:50,792 --> 00:42:53,792
who at the last moment substituted Mara Chekova "

388
00:42:53,917 --> 00:42:56,125
" Sets were uselessly revolutionary . "

389
00:42:56,292 --> 00:42:58,417
" Doubts regarding the direction . "

390
00:42:58,500 --> 00:43:00,173
" Word to the director :

391
00:43:00,208 --> 00:43:02,667
Go back to horror films . Forget opera . "

392
00:43:04,083 --> 00:43:06,083
They 're tearing you to pieces .

393
00:43:06,833 --> 00:43:08,542
Yes , but nicely .

394
00:43:08,667 --> 00:43:10,458
And a total unknown gets all the praise .

395
00:43:10,500 --> 00:43:13,375
Well , she was fantastic .

396
00:43:13,583 --> 00:43:14,840
The last time they said

397
00:43:14,875 --> 00:43:16,167
nice things about your singer

398
00:43:16,333 --> 00:43:18,458
and criticised your direction of Rigoletto

399
00:43:18,500 --> 00:43:21,167
you were furious , but not this time .

400
00:43:21,667 --> 00:43:23,125
How come ?

401
00:43:24,375 --> 00:43:26,548
Tell me the truth

402
00:43:26,583 --> 00:43:28,417
do you want to take the girl to bed ?

403
00:43:29,083 --> 00:43:31,042
Listen . To be here with you this evening ,

404
00:43:31,208 --> 00:43:35,667
I took two flights and turned down a fashion show .

405
00:43:43,083 --> 00:43:46,083
Fragments of the same feathers mixed with traces of blood ...

406
00:43:46,118 --> 00:43:50,500
Were found on a carpet in Stefano Brini 's apartment .

407
00:43:51,792 --> 00:43:53,507
He worked here as your ...

408
00:43:53,542 --> 00:43:59,042
- Stage manager . - Yes . Stage manager .

409
00:44:00,500 --> 00:44:04,833
He was killed , or rather ... butchered last night ,

410
00:44:05,125 --> 00:44:07,042
Between 1 am and 2 am .

411
00:44:07,917 --> 00:44:09,792
Who saw him last ?

412
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:15,542
Well , there was a first-night party .

413
00:44:16,500 --> 00:44:18,000
Did he leave alone ?

414
00:44:18,167 --> 00:44:20,625
I really don 't know . I wasn 't there .

415
00:44:20,708 --> 00:44:23,458
Who else went to the party ? You ?

416
00:44:23,792 --> 00:44:24,792
Yes .

417
00:44:24,875 --> 00:44:28,083
At what time did he leave ? Was he alone ?

418
00:44:28,917 --> 00:44:31,708
I think he left with Betty , our singer .

419
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:34,750
- Where is Betty ? - She should arrive soon .

420
00:44:34,833 --> 00:44:36,292
We 're about to rehearse so if you don 't mind ...

421
00:44:36,375 --> 00:44:38,083
Sorry , I 'm not done yet .

422
00:44:38,917 --> 00:44:40,632
You 're Maurizio , right ?

423
00:44:40,667 --> 00:44:42,583
Are you in charge of the ravens ?

424
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:44,500
- Yes . - How many were killed ?

425
00:44:44,708 --> 00:44:46,090
Three , Inspector .

426
00:44:46,125 --> 00:44:48,375
I think I know who killed my ravens .

427
00:44:48,542 --> 00:44:50,042
- Who ? - Mara Chekova .

428
00:44:50,125 --> 00:44:51,458
That lunatic hated them !

429
00:44:51,542 --> 00:44:54,375
No . Maurizio , that 's nonsense .

430
00:44:54,410 --> 00:44:55,667
Don 't be ridiculous .

431
00:44:55,750 --> 00:44:57,667
Ravens are very vindictive .

432
00:44:57,702 --> 00:44:59,090
They don 't forget .

433
00:44:59,125 --> 00:45:00,798
They remember for years

434
00:45:00,833 --> 00:45:03,083
and at the right moment , zap !

435
00:45:03,208 --> 00:45:04,542
What do you think ?

436
00:45:05,375 --> 00:45:06,708
There were many strange occurrences ...

437
00:45:06,743 --> 00:45:07,917
during this performance ...

438
00:45:07,952 --> 00:45:09,048
What a bore ...

439
00:45:09,083 --> 00:45:11,417
and so many coincidences .

440
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:15,208
I don 't want you to think I 'm superstitious

441
00:45:15,458 --> 00:45:17,500
But it 's Macbeth that brings bad luck .

442
00:45:17,583 --> 00:45:19,167
Everyone knows that .

443
00:45:19,292 --> 00:45:22,250
I could tell you about dozens of strange incidents .

444
00:45:22,458 --> 00:45:24,292
A lot of people seriously believe

445
00:45:24,327 --> 00:45:26,875
that the opera is jinxed .

446
00:45:27,792 --> 00:45:30,007
I 've seen a lot of your movies .

447
00:45:30,042 --> 00:45:32,500
You 're really an expert in this field .

448
00:45:32,667 --> 00:45:35,167
I 'd be very interested to know your opinion .

449
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:37,125
I 'm sorry but I don 't see the point

450
00:45:37,160 --> 00:45:39,000
in using movies to explain the reality .

451
00:45:39,167 --> 00:45:41,083
Depends what you mean by reality .

452
00:45:41,208 --> 00:45:43,167
Excuse me , but I 've got to fix this dress .

453
00:45:43,250 --> 00:45:45,167
The next performance is in two days

454
00:45:45,250 --> 00:45:46,875
and I only have a pair of hands .

455
00:45:47,167 --> 00:45:48,882
Even if you had ten hands

456
00:45:48,917 --> 00:45:50,583
that costume would still be a rag .

457
00:45:50,875 --> 00:45:52,667
What ?

458
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:54,833
All right , Mr. Great Director !

459
00:45:54,917 --> 00:45:56,062
I 'd put most of the blame

460
00:45:56,097 --> 00:45:57,173
for what 's happening ...

461
00:45:57,208 --> 00:45:59,375
On our fancy-pants , whimsical director here ...

462
00:45:59,410 --> 00:46:00,548
who thinks Verdi and Shakespeare

463
00:46:00,583 --> 00:46:02,500
were two incompetent idiots just like him .

464
00:46:02,625 --> 00:46:04,875
I 'll fix the dress , all right , but not for you !

465
00:46:04,910 --> 00:46:07,208
For Giuseppe Verdi !

466
00:46:16,042 --> 00:46:19,208
- All this turns you on , doesn 't it ? - What are you talking about ?

467
00:46:19,292 --> 00:46:21,500
- You 're a sadist . - Oh , really ?

468
00:46:21,625 --> 00:46:24,167
Everyone I know who has worked with you says it .

469
00:46:24,667 --> 00:46:27,333
If they say it , they 're wrong .

470
00:46:52,042 --> 00:46:53,792
Giulia ?

471
00:46:54,333 --> 00:46:55,917
Just the person I wanted to see .

472
00:46:56,083 --> 00:46:58,750
- What 's happened to my costume ? - Look at this mess .

473
00:46:58,833 --> 00:47:01,542
- Someone tore it apart . - Who could have done it ?

474
00:47:01,708 --> 00:47:03,458
I don 't know ... someone who doesn 't like the opera ,

475
00:47:03,500 --> 00:47:05,333
Or Marc 's dreadful representation .

476
00:47:05,417 --> 00:47:08,000
That genius went over the top this time !

477
00:47:08,250 --> 00:47:09,708
It 's not like in the movies

478
00:47:09,750 --> 00:47:11,542
where when you come up with something original

479
00:47:11,625 --> 00:47:14,125
everyone congratulates you .

480
00:47:17,583 --> 00:47:20,542
God , what a mess ! Now , I need to fix it !

481
00:47:20,583 --> 00:47:21,792
And since they didn 't call in the dressmaker

482
00:47:21,827 --> 00:47:23,708
I need to do it myself !

483
00:47:24,083 --> 00:47:25,417
I 'm sorry . You 'll have to try on again

484
00:47:25,452 --> 00:47:26,750
once I 've finished .

485
00:47:31,292 --> 00:47:32,507
We 're lucky , though .

486
00:47:32,542 --> 00:47:34,458
The jewellery is still intact .

487
00:47:34,500 --> 00:47:36,750
Listen , Giulia , I 'll be back in a minute .

488
00:47:59,208 --> 00:48:01,500
Mira , I must see you now .

489
00:48:01,708 --> 00:48:04,875
Me too . My phone hasn 't stopped ringing .

490
00:48:05,167 --> 00:48:07,750
Everybody wants you . Rome ! Vienna ! Paris !

491
00:48:07,792 --> 00:48:09,382
That 's wonderful

492
00:48:09,417 --> 00:48:11,542
but I have to talk to you about something else .

493
00:48:11,667 --> 00:48:13,298
Something really serious .

494
00:48:13,333 --> 00:48:15,417
There 's a maniac who 's after me .

495
00:48:15,500 --> 00:48:18,667
- I need your advice on what to do . - I 'll give it to you now .

496
00:48:18,833 --> 00:48:21,208
- Call the police . - No , I can 't .

497
00:48:21,500 --> 00:48:22,757
I 'm in terrible trouble

498
00:48:22,792 --> 00:48:24,458
and I don 't know what to do .

499
00:48:24,625 --> 00:48:26,917
Mira , I must see you . Come quick , please !

500
00:48:27,250 --> 00:48:29,208
Yeah , all right . I 'll come by this evening .

501
00:48:29,243 --> 00:48:30,333
But what 's going on ?

502
00:48:30,500 --> 00:48:31,500
Betty ?

503
00:49:06,417 --> 00:49:07,500
Betty ?

504
00:49:08,667 --> 00:49:10,125
Is that you ?

505
00:49:23,750 --> 00:49:24,833
Who is it ?

506
00:50:03,167 --> 00:50:05,292
Oh it 's you ! You scared me !

507
00:50:05,327 --> 00:50:06,917
Come here , look .

508
00:50:07,542 --> 00:50:09,208
It was on your costume .

509
00:50:09,333 --> 00:50:10,500
So ?

510
00:50:10,542 --> 00:50:13,375
It 's gold ! I never sewed any real gold on this thing .

511
00:50:13,500 --> 00:50:16,917
- Is it yours ? - No , I never saw it before .

512
00:50:18,333 --> 00:50:21,333
- How did it get on my costume ? - Who knows ?

513
00:50:21,625 --> 00:50:23,750
Maybe the one ripped up the dress dropped it .

514
00:50:23,785 --> 00:50:25,917
Yes and it got caught in the sequins .

515
00:50:26,000 --> 00:50:27,542
Give me that .

516
00:50:28,875 --> 00:50:31,500
It looks like there 's something written on it ...

517
00:50:31,708 --> 00:50:32,895
Maybe a name ...

518
00:50:32,930 --> 00:50:34,083
A name ? Show me !

519
00:50:34,292 --> 00:50:37,375
It 's unreadable . The letters are almost faded away .

520
00:50:38,500 --> 00:50:42,458
Wait , I have a magnifying glass somewhere ...

521
00:50:42,493 --> 00:50:43,875
Where did I see it ?

522
00:50:44,500 --> 00:50:46,542
I can 't remember .

523
00:50:47,458 --> 00:50:48,458
Ah yes !

524
00:50:49,125 --> 00:50:51,583
It should be ...

525
00:50:58,583 --> 00:51:01,125
- Any Luck ? - No !

526
00:51:03,708 --> 00:51:06,167
I 'm sure I had seen it !

527
00:51:07,542 --> 00:51:08,875
Wait , maybe it 's here .

528
00:51:12,917 --> 00:51:14,833
Nothing , nothing ... It disappeared !

529
00:51:17,542 --> 00:51:19,000
What happened ?

530
00:51:19,208 --> 00:51:20,833
- Betty ! ? - I 'm all right !

531
00:51:21,208 --> 00:51:22,667
Don 't worry !

532
00:51:23,375 --> 00:51:25,104
No , no , it can 't be here .

533
00:51:25,139 --> 00:51:26,833
I saw it in a drawer ...

534
00:51:33,542 --> 00:51:35,542
Betty , you continue looking .

